      en: ["One of the two archiepiscopal seats in Hungary since 1001.", "World-famous center for paprika production and research.", "The Kalocsa embroidery is recognized as a traditional Hungaricum.", "The current Cathedral was built in Italian Baroque style in 1735.", "The Archbishop's Library holds over 150,000 volumes and rare codices.", "Home to the world's first Paprika Museum, established in 1972."],
